\n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "From the graph, we see that as we approach $x=2$ from the left, the $y$-value approaches $-1.$ So the left-hand limit is\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\,{2}^{-}}g(x)=-1.\n$$\n\nSimilarly, when we approach $x=2$ from the right, the $y$-value again approaches $-1.$ So the right-hand limit is\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\,{2}^{+}}g(x)=-1.\n$$\n\n \n\nSince both the left and right-hand limits exist and are equal to $-1,$ we conclude that\n\n \n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\,2}g(x)=-1.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-131478/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5e2b72a2-c486-5a7a-a65e-57e83b78f6cc"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-131478"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-131480/field-1/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833" :answer/id #uuid "b8b393a3-03e3-5120-8cfb-6e0479140586" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131480/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "19dbbc6d-a3fc-57af-a2d9-e182df3cff4d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-131480/field-1/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833" :answer-field/choices ["q-131480/field-1/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-131480" :question/id #uuid "c70454df-a8a4-5cee-bf50-c27bbb42d751" :question/math-academy-id "q-131480" :question/is-example false :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13932295/assets/e489437aa3b22a90d71dea3d30ff7a53bb800580775666f97dd4a6cf2db76e6d.png)\n\nThe figure above shows the graphs of the functions $y=f(x)$ and $y=g(x).$\n\nEarlier part 1