                                   \n                            \n                                        $0$\n\nEarlier part 2:\n\nFind ${lim}_{x\\to \\,(-1)}g(x).$ If the limit does not exist, write \"DNE\" (without the quotation marks).\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${lim}_{x\\to \\,(-1)}g(x)=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        DNE\n\nEarlier part 3:\n\nFind ${lim}_{x\\to \\,2}g(x).$ If the limit does not exist, write \"DNE\" (without the quotation marks).\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${lim}_{x\\to 2}g(x)=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-1$\n\nCurrent part:\n\nFind ${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }g(x)$ and ${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }g(x).$ If a limit does not exist, write \"DNE\" (without the quotation marks).\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }g(x)=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                                \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }g(x)=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "On the left side of the graph, we see that as the values of $x$ decrease and approach $-\\infty ,$ the graph of the function $g(x)$ moves closer and closer to the horizontal asymptote $y=3.$\n\nConsequently, $g(x)$ approaches the value $3$ as $x$ approaches $-\\infty ,$ and we have\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }g(x)=3.\n$$\n\nOn the right side of the graph, as the values of $x$ increase and approach $\\infty ,$ the graph of the function decrease without bound to $-\\infty .$   Therefore,\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }g(x)=-\\infty .\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-131479/field-1" "q-131479/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ea4038bf-34f0-58cc-a7b6-6a4c1890570f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-131479"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-131481/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "27881758-ae1e-5e40-8fa3-c1bfd79502e1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131481/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "a1cf3e6d-60c1-5377-9b6e-65a58602d1de" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-131481/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer-field/choices ["q-131481/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-131481" :question/id #uuid "89bd35d8-8c70-5a18-8dc1-54b8d0ae57a0" :question/math-academy-id "q-131481" :question/is-example false :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13932295/assets/e489437aa3b22a90d71dea3d30ff7a53bb800580775666f97dd4a6cf2db76e6d.png)\n\nThe figure above shows the graphs of the functions $y=f(x)$ and $y=g(x).$\n\nEarlier part 1:\n\nFind ${lim}_{x\\to \\,(-1)^{-}}g(x)$ and ${lim}_{x\\to \\,(-1)^{+}}g(x).$ If a limit does not exist, write \"DNE\" (without the quotation marks).\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${lim}_{x\\to \\,(-1)^{-}}g(x)=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $2$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                                \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${lim}_{x\\to \\,(-1)^{+}}g(x)=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $0$\n\nEarlier part 2:\n\nFind ${lim}_{x\\to \\,(-1)}g(x).$ If the limit does not exist, write \"DNE\" (without the quotation marks).\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${lim}_{x\\to \\,(-1)}g(x)=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        DNE\n\nEarlier part 3:\n\nFind ${lim}_{x\\to \\,2}g(x).$ If the limit does not exist, write \"DNE\" (without the quotation marks).\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${lim}_{x\\to 2}g(x)=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-1$\n\nEarlier part 4:\n\nFind ${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }g(x)$ and ${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }g(x).$ If a limit does not exist, write \"DNE\" (without the quotation marks).\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }g(x)=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $3$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                                \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }g(x)=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-\\infty$\n\nEarlier part 5:\n\nGiven that ${lim}_{x\\to \\,2}Cf(x)=\\frac{4}{3},$ where $C$ is a real constant, what is the value of $C?$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $C=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $\\frac{1}{3}$\n\nCurrent part:\n\nEvaluate ${lim}_{x\\to \\,2}(7f(x)+8g(x)-2{x}^{3}).$ If the limit does not exist, write \"DNE\" (without the quotation marks).\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${lim}_{x\\to \\,2}(7f(x)+8g(x)-2{x}^{3})=$ \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "According to the sum and constant multiple rules, we can compute the required limit as follows:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\,2}(7f(x)+8g(x)-2{x}^{3})=7{lim}_{x\\to \\,2}f(x)+8{lim}_{x\\to \\,2}g(x)-2{lim}_{x\\to \\,2}{x}^{3}\n$$\n\n  \n\nThe above equation assumes that ${lim}_{x\\to \\,2}f(x)$ and ${lim}_{x\\to \\,2}g(x)$ both exist.\n\nIn part 5, we found that ${lim}_{x\\to \\,2}f(x)=4,$ and from part 3, we found ${lim}_{x\\to \\,2}g(x)=-1.$ So, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,2}(7f(x)+8g(x)-2{x}^{3}) & =7{lim}_{x\\to \\,2}f(x)+8{lim}_{x\\to \\,2}g(x)-2{lim}_{x\\to \\,2}{x}^{3} \\\\  & =7\\cdot 4+8\\cdot (-1)-2\\cdot {2}^{3} \\\\  & =28-8-16 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-131481/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "38e6d549-0d5a-56e3-88b0-0b22dceb2d0d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-131481"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
